    Forked from upstream release v26.1.2 (commit 3aae65f46a72, tagged
    2026-02-22). Upstream was archived on 2026-05-12 and is no longer
    maintained; the copy in this repository is a permanent hard fork, not a
    vendored snapshot tracking an upstream branch.

    MODIFIED. This copy diverges substantially from upstream v26.1.2 and must
    not be assumed interchangeable with it. Changes were made first in the
    mojo-siren-grail repository (28 commits, from 2026-02-26) and continued
    here (14 commits, from 2026-03-18), and include:

      - Security hardening against request smuggling, slowloris, and integer
        overflow in request parsing
      - Production hardening: connection timeouts, observability hooks,
        response caching, concurrency limits
      - epoll_event struct layout corrected on non-x86_64 targets; accept
        queue drain fix
      - Nullable epoll/timerfd FFI parameters modeled as Optional
      - Null UnsafePointer construction via unsafe_from_address=0
      - Forward compatibility with Mojo 1.1; migration off deprecated
        memory/origin APIs

